1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,308
Strike: weekly options vaults for Robinhood Chain stock tokens.

2
00:00:03,308 --> 00:00:08,140
Live on Robinhood Chain testnet: real events, read from the chain.

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:11,423
Stock tokens on Robinhood Chain earn nothing on their own.

4
00:00:11,423 --> 00:00:14,424
Options exist on the chain, but people run them by hand.

5
00:00:14,424 --> 00:00:17,645
Strike: an AI agent runs the vault, and the contract enforces the rules.

6
00:00:17,645 --> 00:00:23,529
Stonkhouse and Archer Markets: traders pick strikes and trade them on an order book.

7
00:00:23,529 --> 00:00:28,848
In Strike a bonded agent proposes the strike, and the contract checks it.

8
00:00:28,848 --> 00:00:32,170
The playground asks the deployed EpochManager about a proposal: a read-only call, no wallet.

9
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:35,038
Honest agent: a 0.20-delta call. The contract answers: Accepted.

10
00:00:35,038 --> 00:00:38,876
Reckless agent: an at-the-money put. Rejected: DeltaOutOfBand.

11
00:00:38,876 --> 00:00:43,217
The slash: 10 USDG of the agent's bond, paid to the vault's depositors.

12
00:00:43,217 --> 00:00:46,464
A real epoch on Robinhood Chain testnet, 29 Sep 2026. First, the seller agent.

13
00:00:46,464 --> 00:00:48,266
The seller agent targets a 0.20-delta call on the TSLA covered-call vault.

14
00:00:48,266 --> 00:00:49,977
proposeByDelta: the contract solves the strike on-chain.

15
00:00:49,977 --> 00:00:53,418
Accepted at a $369.86 strike. The series goes on sale.

16
00:00:53,418 --> 00:00:57,989
--reckless: the agent forces an at-the-money put, outside the 0.10 to 0.35 delta band.

17
00:00:57,989 --> 00:01:00,002
Rejected on-chain: DeltaOutOfBand. 10 USDG of the agent's bond is slashed.

18
00:01:00,002 --> 00:01:02,006
The agent's bond drops from 60 to 50 USDG: 1 of 3 strikes.

19
00:01:02,006 --> 00:01:06,307
The rejection on Blockscout: proposeSeries, and 10 USDG moved out of the agent's bond.

20
00:01:06,307 --> 00:01:10,633
A buyer agent spends up to 15 USDG on the live series.

21
00:01:10,633 --> 00:01:13,177
It bought 4 calls for 10.005944 USDG. The premium is the most it can lose.

22
00:01:13,177 --> 00:01:17,063
The TSLA covered-call vault on testnet: a call at $369.86, expiring Fri Oct 2. All 4 sold.

23
00:01:17,063 --> 00:01:22,891
The buy price: spot plus 0.5% against the buyer, at Black-Scholes fair value, never below intrinsic.

24
00:01:22,891 --> 00:01:28,422
Buyer profits above $372.36. At or below $369.86, depositors keep the full premium.

25
00:01:28,422 --> 00:01:31,763
The backtest: 403 weekly epochs, Jan 2019 to Sep 2026, run by the contract rules.

26
00:01:31,763 --> 00:01:35,367
NVDA: the covered call's volatility is 26.5%, against 45.6% for holding the stock.

27
00:01:35,367 --> 00:01:42,303
A covered call trades upside for 25 to 46% lower volatility, on every stock tested.

28
00:01:42,303 --> 00:01:44,788
Every agent posts a USDG bond. A rejected proposal costs 10 USDG.

29
00:01:44,788 --> 00:01:49,930
Agent #1: ERC-8004 identity #114, 1 accepted, 1 rejected, 1 strike, 50 USDG bond.

30
00:01:49,930 --> 00:01:53,562
The rejection feed: DeltaOutOfBand on the TSLA put vault, 10 USDG slashed.

31
00:01:53,562 --> 00:02:01,096
An open market: any agent can register, bond USDG and run a vault.

32
00:02:01,096 --> 00:02:03,841
The Telegram bot reads the chain's logs and posts an alert for each event.

33
00:02:03,841 --> 00:02:07,671
A rejected proposal: the rule it broke, the 10 USDG slash and the transaction.

34
00:02:07,671 --> 00:02:10,823
A sale: 4 TSLA calls bought for 10.005944 USDG.

35
00:02:10,823 --> 00:02:13,506
The safety monitor: every Robinhood Chain stock token, read live from mainnet.

36
00:02:13,506 --> 00:02:16,921
Each token gets the verdict the contracts would give: five checks, or no price.

37
00:02:16,921 --> 00:02:21,454
NVDA's multiplier is 1.000775159: already in the price, so Strike never applies it.

38
00:02:21,454 --> 00:02:22,438
The proof page: every claim next to its evidence.

39
00:02:22,438 --> 00:02:25,369
Every deployed contract is verified on Blockscout.

40
00:02:25,369 --> 00:02:28,389
432 Foundry tests, plus Rust, TypeScript, bot and subgraph tests.

41
00:02:28,389 --> 00:02:31,420
9 properties proven with Halmos, for every input in range.

42
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:34,568
An internal review: 11 findings, all fixed, with regression tests.

43
00:02:34,568 --> 00:02:39,651
802 tests and proofs: 432 Foundry tests, 9 fork tests on mainnet, 9 Halmos proofs, and more.

44
00:02:39,651 --> 00:02:44,052
99.1% line coverage and 97.5% branch coverage, above the 95% CI gate.

45
00:02:44,052 --> 00:02:48,173
The strike solver in Stylus costs 6.5× less gas than in Solidity.

46
00:02:48,173 --> 00:02:51,436
Strike: options on Robinhood Chain, run by agents that cannot break the rules.

47
00:02:51,436 --> 00:02:54,698
802 tests and proofs (432 Foundry tests), 9 invariants, 9 formal proofs, fork tests on mainnet. github.com/Prashant-thakur77/Strike
